  "$comment": "Clients additionally validate exact references/kinds, ordered level subsets, reference membership, metadata report consistency, duplicate keys, finite values and path containment. Legacy files without design remain schema 0.1.0; first set_design promotes to 0.2.0. No scientific validation. Dataset scope and DATA design pins require schema 0.3.0. Clients validate reference kinds and canonical scope/report evidence; no implicit scientific verification. Schema 0.4.0 adds explicit input mode and captured figure preservation; context consistency is checked on new or revised analytical context, not legacy load. Optional approved_renderers_v1 figure policy and reserved locally observed renderer receipts require schema 0.4.0; clients validate receipt output hash binding. No scientific acceptance or unrestricted-interpreter security boundary. Clients additionally check export_settings pixel-area bound and binding to FIG details.format.",
